## SQ-FDI-01 | Carrot Edition loads, no parse error, Food Dictionary item
@group A
@commands After the jar is in `mods/`: boot; `grep -n "solcarrot\|Failed to parse" logs/latest.log`; `/give @s solcarrot:food_book`
@pass mod loads, no parse errors; item named Food Dictionary
@fails check `defaultconfigs/solcarrot-server.toml` parses (milestones list)
@from batches/r1113/c4_a.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)Failed to parse.*solcarrot|solcarrot.*(exception|could not)
shell grep -nE "solcarrot|Failed to parse" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-250 | head -20; ls mods | grep -iE "carrot|raspberry"; true
> cdevtest item solcarrot:food_book
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=item done= 30
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=item item=solcarrot:food_book class=
look item name "Food Dictionary" is a lang check (client); here: the item exists and the mod loaded without errors

