## CQ-FDI-01
@group client
@commands Open the Food Dictionary uneaten pages with client config `[foodDictionary] uneatenSort` = MOD_NAME (default), then NAME, EASIEST, HARDEST (save, reopen the book each time) (plan 2.2)
@pass MOD_NAME: grouped by mod id, A-Z by name inside; NAME: A-Z by name; EASIEST: lowest Apple Pie complexity first (simple foods such as apples before meals), ties by lower nutrition; HARDEST: the reverse
@fails `FoodDictionarySort.uneaten`, `CarrotFoodDataMixin`
@draft written before the look-check (plan_diet_books.md 3); refresh after it

## CQ-FDI-02
@group client
@commands Food Dictionary: page through it; on an eaten-foods page click the sort button (top right) three times, hovering it each time (plan 2.3)
@pass the button shows only on the eaten-foods pages; states cycle newest unlock (golden carrot), latest eaten (clock), uneaten order (book), back to newest unlock; the tooltip names the state; the list re-sorts in place on the same page; the state is saved in `[foodDictionary] eatenSort` and kept after closing the book
@fails `CarrotBookScreenMixin` (`solrp$addSortButton`, `solrp$updateSortButton`, eaten page range), `FoodDictionarySort.cycleEaten`
@draft written before the look-check (plan_diet_books.md 3); refresh after it

## CQ-FDI-03
@group client
@commands In a world with foods unlocked before this jar: eat two new foods A then B; re-eat an old food C; check each sort state; relog; die and respawn (plan 2.3)
@pass newest unlock: B, A first, then the older unlocks in the uneaten order; latest eaten: C first, then B, A, foods Apple Pie no longer remembers last in the uneaten order; uneaten order: the uneatenSort order; the order survives relog and death
@fails `CarrotFoodListMixin` (NBT `solrp_unlockOrder`), `FoodDictionarySort.eaten`
@draft written before the look-check (plan_diet_books.md 3); refresh after it

## CQ-FDI-04
@group client
@commands Food Dictionary: scroll the mouse wheel down and up past both ends (plan 2.3, as 1.6)
@pass one page per notch with a page turn sound, nothing past either end; the sort button appears and hides with the page
@fails `CarrotBookScreenMixin.mouseScrolled`
@draft written before the look-check (plan_diet_books.md 3); refresh after it
